              }
            ],
            "id": "zz9ew3alfu5kqnf",
            "rowstyle": "alternating",
            "type": "table"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "We find that during the first half-life (from 0.00 hours to 6.00 hours), the concentration of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " decreases from 1.000 M to 0.500 M. During the second half-life (from 6.00 hours to 12.00 hours), it decreases from 0.500 M to 0.250 M; during the third half-life, it decreases from 0.250 M to 0.125 M. The concentration of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " decreases by half during each successive period of 6.00 hours. The decomposition of hydrogen peroxide is a first-order reaction, and, as shown below, the half-life of a first-order reaction is independent of the concentration of the reactant. It is worth noting that half-lives of reactions with other orders depend on the concentrations of the reactants."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3st4yhyb8z6a6w7",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The equation for determining the half-life of a first-order reaction can be derived from the integrated rate law. In previous examples, we have rearranged the integrated rate law to solve for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              }
            ],
            "id": "olk5pskp7p4jui6",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "3ghv5qt2418vu59",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "34ztlkl2tkc30rr",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "t\\;=\\;\\frac1k\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\lbrack A\\rbrack_0}{{\\lbrack A\\rbrack}_t}\\right)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "If we set the time, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": ", equal to the half-life, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the corresponding concentration of A, [A]"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": ", at this time is equal to one-half of its initial concentration. Therefore, when "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": " = "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", we have "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_t\\;=\\;\\frac12{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_0",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "0bqp3f2w90xk8l6",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Substituting in these values and simplifying gives:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "9zaw4e6zvf6pwwg",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "4zkw1sspw6yjwdv",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "yjj386y11xjx61r",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "t_{1/2}\\;=\\;\\frac1k\\ln\\left(\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0}{\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0}\\right)\\; =\\;\\frac1k\\left(\\ln\\,2\\;\\right)\\;=\\;\\frac1k\\left(0.693\\right)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "025c22oleplj1lu",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "xxpzgbkfzjzxzcz",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "t_{1/2}\\;=\\;\\frac{0.693}k",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "We can see that the half-life of a first-order reaction is "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "inversely proportional"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "As one variable increases, another variable decreases at the same rate, and vice versa. "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1589038237",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1738664333",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " to the rate constant "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "k"
              },
              {
                "text": ". A faster reaction (shorter half-life) will have a larger "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "k"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and a slower reaction (longer half-life) will have a smaller "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "k"
              },
              {
                "text": ". We also see that "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": " for a first-order reaction does not depend on concentration."
              }
            ],
            "id": "0bug2wmppbh2qj6",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2757776051",
        "selection": {
