      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Calculate the rate constant for the first-order decomposition of hydrogen peroxide in water at 40 °C, using the data given in the following figure."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "22b5ekq1cnx1kgj",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "alt": "A diagram of 5 beakers is shown, each approximately half-filled with colored substances. Beneath each beaker are three rows of text. \n                        The first beaker contains a bright green substance and is labeled below as, “1.000 M, 0 s, and ( 0 h ).” The second beaker contains a \n                        slightly lighter green substance and is labeled below as, “0.500 M, 2.16 times 10 superscript 4 s, and ( 6 h ).” The third beaker contains \n                        an even lighter green substance and is labeled below as, “0.250 M, 4.32 times 10 superscript 4 s, and ( 12 h ).” The fourth beaker contains \n                        a green tinted substance and is labeled below as, “0.125 M, 6.48 times 10 superscript 4 s, and ( 18 h ).” The fifth beaker contains a \n                        colorless substance and is labeled below as, “0.0625 M, 8.64 times 10 superscript 4 s, and ( 24 h ).”",
                "caption": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "The decomposition of H"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": " (2 H"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": " "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                        "src": "\\longrightarrow",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": " 2 H"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "O + O"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": ") at 40 °C is illustrated. The intensity of the color symbolizes the concentration of H"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": " at the indicated times; H"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "O"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": " is actually colorless."
                      }
                    ],
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "79s02ac76fyjglx",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ykze293fvs42k99",
                "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/0d/0d837007d74749097674b7be697131ac/CNX_Chem_12_04_HPerDcmp.jpg",
                "type": "img",
                "width": "650"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Half of the H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is consumed every 2.16 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " s, which means that the half-life for the decomposition of H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is 2.16 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " s. We first rearrange the first-order half-life relationship to solve for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "k"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ifb856o0bxlue6f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "xciuf2mua18mnn5",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3za6i1baviloygb",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "t_{1/2}\\;=\\;\\frac{0.693}k\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;k\\;=\\;\\frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "and then substitute the value for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "t"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "1/2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " to determine the rate constant value:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "5tbnq7j9qr8eu76",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "wlu8l0if5bz5igh",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "kj9y1zz6k1z5bnt",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "k\\;=\\;\\frac{0.693}{t_{1/2}}\\;=\\;\\frac{0.693}{2.16\\times10^4\\;\\mathrm s}\\;=\\;3.21\\times10^{-5}\\;\\mathrm s^{-1}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2850391434",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
