      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "6y43upe5dojrtyt",
                "text": "Half-Life of Second-Order Reactions"
              }
            ],
            "id": "pr5ye8w5h1tilim",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Following the same approach as used for first-order reactions, we derive the equation for determining the half-life of a second-order reaction by starting with its integrated rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "f20slr93vkj918o",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ihzqjujgp9pamw3",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "q2c730lvzpocng9",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\frac1{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t}\\;=\\;kt\\;+\\;\\frac1{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When the initial concentration, [A]"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "0"
              },
              {
                "text": ", has decreased to half of its original value, we have "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": " = "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{{t}_{1/2}}=\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "mvj30igpbb0er38",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Substitute these values into the second-order integrated rate law, then simplify and solve for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "\\frac1{\\frac12{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}\\;\\;=\\;kt_{1/2}\\;+\\;\\frac1{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "\\frac1{\\frac12{\\lbrack A\\rbrack}_0\\;}\\;-\\;\\frac1{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}\\;=\\;kt_{1/2}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "\\frac2{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}\\;\\;-\\;\\frac1{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}=\\;kt_{1/2}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "\\frac1{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}=\\;kt_{1/2}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                "src": "t_{1/2\\;}=\\;\\frac1{k{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_0}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": "For a second-order reaction, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": " is inversely proportional to the concentration of the reactant (not to the rate constant, as is the case for first-order reactions). The half-life increases as the reaction proceeds because the concentration of reactant decreases. Unlike with first-order reactions, the half-life of a second-order reaction is not actually a constant for the reaction and instead depends on the (initial) concentration."
              }
            ],
            "id": "pmzadpgb8oo79mk",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "4264618975",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "activity_id": 78762,
            "id": "2344151384",
            "type": "activity-reference"
          }
        ],
        "id": "645931327",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "learnbydoing",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "10ttm6xgcgwt19n",
                "text": "Half-Life of Zero-Order Reactions"
              }
            ],
            "id": "xydqwg678wi28d1",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "We can also derive the equation for the half-life of a zero-order reaction by starting with its integrated rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "n7lgor63peedy6s",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "c0pmctfartfuuh4",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2npx94uqfaxf5h5",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_t\\;=\\;-kt\\;+\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When the initial concentration, [A]"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "0"
              },
              {
                "text": ", has decreased to half of its original value, we have "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": " = "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{{t}_{1/2}}=\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "9u70mgghk70v8nl",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Substitute these values into the zero-order integrated rate law:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "o1pfcl84pmzsxzg",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "k2jzoznr9qbvmtp",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "g3n44jy15d1eomx",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0\\;=\\;-kt_{1/2}\\;+\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Rearrange and solve for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1/2"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              }
            ],
            "id": "jzf0iurq5t1wp65",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "8e3rd4dnhsovby4",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "8y2balw7ooircgy",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "kt_{1/2}\\;=\\;\\;\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0\\;-\\;\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0\\;=\\;\\frac12\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0\\; =\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0}2",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "67jniqs82s13nqk",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "npsqehgkh0rn369",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "t_{1/2}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack_0}{2k}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The half-life of a zero-order reaction is not constant; it is proportional to the initial concentration."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ggko5rfjo4q9nqg",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
